# Deployment & CI/CD Rules

Full guide: [docs/DEPLOYMENT.md](mdc:docs/DEPLOYMENT.md). Keep it in sync when changing anything below.

## 🚀 Where things run

- **Frontend**: Cloudflare Pages (Git integration builds `resume-builder/`). `main` → https://presmistique.in; other branches → preview URLs on `*.resume-builder-6rc.pages.dev`. No GitHub Actions involvement.
- **Backend**: Docker container on an Ubuntu VPS, behind host nginx (Let's Encrypt TLS) at https://api.presmistique.in → `127.0.0.1:5000`.
- **Images**: GitHub Container Registry, `ghcr.io/<owner>/presmistique-api:sha-<7char>` and `:latest`.
- **Database**: MongoDB Atlas in production; throwaway local MongoDB in local Docker dev.

## 📁 Key files

- **CI**: [.github/workflows/ci.yml](mdc:.github/workflows/ci.yml)
- **API deploy**: [.github/workflows/deploy-backend.yml](mdc:.github/workflows/deploy-backend.yml)
- **Production stack**: [deploy/docker-compose.yml](mdc:deploy/docker-compose.yml) + [deploy/deploy.sh](mdc:deploy/deploy.sh) (copied to `/opt/presmistique` on every deploy)
- **Backend image**: [backend/Dockerfile](mdc:backend/Dockerfile), [backend/.dockerignore](mdc:backend/.dockerignore)
- **Local dev stack**: [docker-compose.yml](mdc:docker-compose.yml) (API + local MongoDB)
- **Puppeteer launch options**: [backend/utils/browserManager.js](mdc:backend/utils/browserManager.js) → `getLaunchOptions()`

## ✅ CI (`ci.yml`)

Runs on PRs to `main`/`dev`, pushes to `dev`, and manual runs. Never deploys.
- `changes`: `dorny/paths-filter` → backend (`backend/**`, `deploy/**`, `.github/workflows/**`) / frontend (`resume-builder/**`, `.github/workflows/**`).
- `backend` (Node 22): `npm ci`, `node --check` on every tracked JS file, `npm test` (unit tests plus MongoDB-backed token and payment tests), `bash -n deploy/deploy.sh`.
- `backend-image`: builds `backend/Dockerfile`, smoke-tests that Chromium launches via `getLaunchOptions()` and renders a PDF.
- `frontend`: `npm ci` + `npm run build` with Node from `resume-builder/.nvmrc`.
- `ci-passed`: the single check required by branch protection on `main` (skipped jobs count as passed).

## 🚢 Backend deploy (`deploy-backend.yml`)

- Trigger: push to `main` touching `backend/**`, `deploy/**` or the workflow; or manual run.
- Build job: builds `backend/Dockerfile`, pushes `sha-<7char>` + `latest` to GHCR using `GITHUB_TOKEN`.
- Deploy job (environment `production`): SSH with a dedicated deploy key + pinned known_hosts, `scp` compose file and `deploy.sh` to `/opt/presmistique`, `docker login ghcr.io`, run `deploy.sh <tag>`, logout, then public `curl https://api.presmistique.in/health`.
- `deploy.sh <tag>`: writes `API_IMAGE` + `IMAGE_TAG` to `.env`, `docker compose pull api` + `up -d`, polls `http://127.0.0.1:5000/health` (~90 s), auto-rolls back to the previous tag on failure, keeps only current + previous images.
- Manual run with `image_tag` input = rollback/redeploy an existing tag (build is skipped).
- Required secrets: `VPS_HOST`, `VPS_USER`, `VPS_SSH_KEY`, `VPS_KNOWN_HOSTS`.

## 🐳 Backend image rules

- Base `node:22-bookworm-slim` + Debian `chromium` and fonts; **not Alpine**.
- `PUPPETEER_EXECUTABLE_PATH=/usr/bin/chromium`, `PUPPETEER_SKIP_DOWNLOAD=true`.
- Every `puppeteer.launch()` must use `getLaunchOptions()` from `backend/utils/browserManager.js`. Locally (no `PUPPETEER_EXECUTABLE_PATH`) Puppeteer uses its own downloaded Chrome.
- Runs as non-root `node`; `CMD ["node", "server.js"]`; only `logs/` and `uploads/` are written at runtime (mounted from `/opt/presmistique/data/`).
- `npm ci --omit=dev`: anything needed at runtime must be in `dependencies`.
- Health endpoint `GET /health` is used by the Docker `HEALTHCHECK`, `deploy.sh` and the workflow — keep it fast and dependency-free.

## 🔐 Environment & secrets

- **Production API secrets**: `/opt/presmistique/api.env` on the VPS (chmod 600, never committed). `NODE_ENV`/`PORT` come from the compose file. Variable reference: [backend/env.template](mdc:backend/env.template).
- **`/opt/presmistique/.env`**: only `API_IMAGE` and `IMAGE_TAG`, written by `deploy.sh`.
- **Frontend**: `REACT_APP_*` variables in Cloudflare Pages project settings (public, baked in at build time). Production `REACT_APP_API_URL=https://api.presmistique.in/api`.
- **Local**: `backend/.env`, `resume-builder/.env` (from the `env.template` files).

## 🛠️ Commands

```bash
# Local dev
docker compose up --build              # API (production image) + local MongoDB on :5000
cd backend && npm run dev              # API with nodemon (needs your own MongoDB)
cd resume-builder && npm start         # frontend on :3000

# On the VPS, from /opt/presmistique
./deploy.sh sha-1a2b3c4                # deploy/rollback to a tag
docker compose logs -f --tail 200 api
docker compose restart api
docker compose up -d --force-recreate api       # after editing api.env
docker compose exec api npm run <script>        # admin scripts (unlock-account, add-tokens, seed:all-templates)
```

## 🔄 Rollback

- **API**: Actions → Deploy API → Run workflow with `image_tag=sha-xxxxxxx`, or `./deploy.sh sha-xxxxxxx` on the server.
- **Frontend**: Cloudflare Pages → Deployments → Rollback.
- **Database**: MongoDB Atlas backups / point-in-time recovery.

## 📋 Checklist when changing deployment

1. Update `ci.yml` smoke tests if the image or Puppeteer setup changes.
2. Keep `deploy/docker-compose.yml` volume paths in sync with what the app writes.
3. New runtime env vars → `backend/env.template` and the server's `api.env`.
4. Update [docs/DEPLOYMENT.md](mdc:docs/DEPLOYMENT.md).
